<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere.  <br>
<I>Solution C:</I> <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NaHCO<sub>3</sub>                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components, filter-sterilize and store under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture.  <br>
To complete the medium, combine Solutions A, B, C and 1 ml Vitamin solution (see below) aseptically under a stream of a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture. Distribute the medium into sterilized culture vessels under the same gas mixture and seal with butyl rubber stoppers. Then, add 0.01 volume of 5% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution (autoclaved under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere). Check the final pH to be 7.0 - 7.2. Pressurize the inoculated vessels to 70 kPa N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) overpressure.  <br>
<I>Vitamin solution:</I>   <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Biotin                                                 </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;20.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
